invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_vaes.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_vaes.h's gcm_use_vaes answers 0 whatever the key's session
  stated, so no key runs the VAES kernels and CH_CPU_VAES picks nothing.
  Every vector passes, because the 128-bit loops compute the same bytes;
  only the time is wrong. The script compiles gcm.c for x86-64 and
  requires its object to call the three kernels.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0 && (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 0;
